Working around the scanner with manual manifest entry
It found the right site this time (it says “Missing Name” instead of “GitHub”), but the problem is your HTML file is ~97KB — PWABuilder’s scanner is timing out before it can parse through the whole page to find the manifest link. That’s a PWABuilder limitation, not a problem with your code.

The fix is simple — just click “Edit Your Manifest” and fill it in manually:

Info tab:

Name: Blood Trail Finder
Short Name: Blood Trail
Description: Use your phone camera to detect and track deer blood trails while hunting.
Id: /blood-trail/
Settings tab:

Start URL: /blood-trail/
Scope: /blood-trail/
Display: standalone
Orientation: portrait
Background Color: 
#0e100b
Theme Color: 
#0e100b
Icons tab:

Upload or point to your icons at:
https://stantonidel.github.io/blood-trail/icon-192.png (192×192, any)
https://stantonidel.github.io/blood-trail/icon-512.png (512×512, any)
https://stantonidel.github.io/blood-trail/icon-192-maskable.png (192×192, maskable)
https://stantonidel.github.io/blood-trail/icon-512-maskable.png (512×512, maskable)
Once you’ve filled those in, PWABuilder will let you click “Package For Stores” and generate your .aab file. Your manifest.json is on GitHub and works fine — the scanner just can’t handle parsing the big HTML file fast enough.

